<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/basal-bolus-insulin-regime-for-inpatients-with-variable-food-intake> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Basal Bolus insulin regime for inpatients with variable food intake" ;
    dmo:populationScope "inpatients with variable food intake" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "basal-bolus-insulin-regime-for-inpatients-with-variable-food-intake" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Basal Bolus - Here a background insulin is supplemented by rapid insulin given at meal times. This regime is flexible and allows for mealtimes to be varied, but timing of insulin to meals is essential. For inpatients, if staff on the wards are able to administer this with dose changes being reviewed frequently this can be quite effective in maintaining control where food intake is variable. However, it requires multiple injections a day and can often be too complex for frail elderly patients to maintain or for inexperienced staff to adjust appropriately" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Basal Bolus - Here a background insulin is supplemented by rapid insulin given at meal times. This regime is flexible and allows for mealtimes to be varied, but timing of insulin to meals is essential. For inpatients, if staff on the wards are able to administer this with dose changes being reviewed frequently this can be quite effective in maintaining control where food intake is variable. However, it requires multiple injections a day and can often be too complex for frail elderly patients to maintain or for inexperienced staff to adjust appropriately" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/basal-only-insulin-regime-for-frail-elderly-patients> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Basal Only insulin regime for frail elderly patients" ;
    dmo:populationScope "frail elderly population" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "basal-only-insulin-regime-for-frail-elderly-patients" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Basal Only - where a background insulin is used either on its own or in addition with oral agents. This is often used in patients for whom avoidance of symptoms of hyperglycaemia and hypoglycaemia is the primary aim and for whom a simple regime allows safety to be ensured but where tight targets are not required for long term prevention of complications and as such are often used in the frail elderly population" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Basal Only - where a background insulin is used either on its own or in addition with oral agents. This is often used in patients for whom avoidance of symptoms of hyperglycaemia and hypoglycaemia is the primary aim and for whom a simple regime allows safety to be ensured but where tight targets are not required for long term prevention of complications and as such are often used in the frail elderly population" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

