<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/focused-assessment-of-physical-and-cognitive-domains-during-hospital-admission> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Focused assessment of physical and cognitive domains during hospital admission" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "older people with diabetes and frailty admitted to hospital" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "focused-assessment-of-physical-and-cognitive-domains-during-hospital-admission" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "clinicians should conduct a focused assessment of both physical and cognitive domains during the course of admission as this will assist the clinician in making decisions about the functional status and comorbidity level of inpatients which in turn will guide management" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "clinicians will need to adopt a new set of outcome measures in the management of frailty in diabetes both in hospital settings and in the community and primary care. Apart from glycaemia targets, other key outcomes that require assessment but usually are not a feature of every day diabetes clinical practice are physical performance measures, an objective assessment of hypoglycaemia risk, falls risk assessment, and quality of life: these outcome measures will prove to have an important influence in deciding if a specific management strategy is worthwhile in routine clinical care of older people with diabetes and frailty." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

