<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/individualised-care-plan-prior-to-hospital-admission> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Individualised care plan prior to hospital admission" ;
    dmo:populationScope "older inpatients with frailty and diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "individualised-care-plan-prior-to-hospital-admission" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "There should be a clear action plan when the readings are out of target. This may require a consensus among primary care, secondary care clinicians, care home managers (for residents of care homes) and patients and carers. The document should clarify triggers that prompt a call to the diabetes specialist team or GP. Closer coordination with community-based pharmacists is encouraged." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "There should be a clear action plan when the readings are out of target. This may require a consensus among primary care, secondary care clinicians, care home managers (for residents of care homes) and patients and carers. The document should clarify triggers that prompt a call to the diabetes specialist team or GP . Closer coordination with community-based pharmacists is encouraged." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/individualised-care-plans-for-older-patients-with-diabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Individualised care plans for older patients with diabetes" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Older patients with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "individualised-care-plans-for-older-patients-with-diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Individualised care plans detailing co-morbidities, presence of frailty or functional loss (including cognition), individualised agreed goals of treatment plan, medications, frequency of monitoring, agreed target capillary blood glucose (CBG) when appropriate, with HbA1c, blood pressure and serum cholesterol levels being helpful in some cases" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Individualised care plans detailing co-morbidities, presence of frailty or functional loss (including cognition), individualised agreed goals of treatment plan, medications, frequency of monitoring, agreed target capillary blood glucose (CBG) when appropriate, with HbA1c, blood pressure and serum cholesterol levels being helpful in some cases" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

