<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/premixed-insulins-for-patients-with-fixed-food-and-activity-regime> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Premixed insulins for patients with fixed food and activity regime" ;
    dmo:populationScope "patients with a more fixed food and activity regime" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "premixed-insulins-for-patients-with-fixed-food-and-activity-regime" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Premixed insulins - These insulins contain mixtures of fast acting and intermediate acting insulin in set proportions which is designated in their names. The contents may be either human or analogue insulins and this needs to be taken into account when timing injections. They are most often used twice daily (occasionally three times a day) and are used when patients have a more fixed food and activity regime. If patients are admitted on such regimes, they may not be suitable during times of illness when appetite may be variable and the risk of hypoglycaemia is increased if meals are missed" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Premixed insulins - These insulins contain mixtures of fast acting and intermediate acting insulin in set proportions which is designated in their names. The contents may be either human or analogue insulins and this needs to be taken into account when timing injections. They are most often used twice daily (occasionally three times a day) and are used when patients have a more fixed food and activity regime. If patients are admitted on such regimes, they may not be suitable during times of illness when appetite may be variable and the risk of hypoglycaemia is increased if meals are missed" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

