<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/meal-times-different-to-those-in-community> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Meal Times Different to Those in Community" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Altered meal timing compared to community routine can affect glucose control." ;
    dmo:name "Meal Times Different to Those in Community" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "meal-times-different-to-those-in-community" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "meal times different to those in community, lack of access to snacks" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/meal-timings-that-are-not-co-ordinated-with-insulin-doses> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Meal Timings That Are Not Co-ordinated With Insulin Doses" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The mechanisms that may increase the risk of hypoglycaemia in frail older people include iatrogenic factors, which include: inappropriate types/doses of glucose lowering therapies; medicine errors; meal timings that are not co-ordinated with insulin doses; and a failure to review medicines or set appropriate glucose targets10." ;
    dmo:name "Meal Timings That Are Not Co-ordinated With Insulin Doses" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "meal-timings-that-are-not-co-ordinated-with-insulin-doses" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The mechanisms that may increase the risk of hypoglycaemia in frail older people include iatrogenic factors, which include: inappropriate types/doses of glucose lowering therapies; medicine errors; meal timings that are not co-ordinated with insulin doses; and a failure to review medicines or set appropriate glucose targets10." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/medicine-errors> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Medicine Errors" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The mechanisms that may increase the risk of hypoglycaemia in frail older people include iatrogenic factors, which include: inappropriate types/doses of glucose lowering therapies; medicine errors; meal timings that are not co-ordinated with insulin doses; and a failure to review medicines or set appropriate glucose targets10." ;
    dmo:name "Medicine Errors" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "medicine-errors" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The mechanisms that may increase the risk of hypoglycaemia in frail older people include iatrogenic factors, which include: inappropriate types/doses of glucose lowering therapies; medicine errors; meal timings that are not co-ordinated with insulin doses; and a failure to review medicines or set appropriate glucose targets10." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Medicine errors are still too high in hospitalised diabetes patients, and in those who are frail and especially those with communication deficits these risks may be amplified." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/medicines-prescribing-and-administration-errors> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Medicines Prescribing and Administration Errors" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "An ongoing cause of concern and a major risk factor for frail older people with diabetes is the incidence of prescribing and administration errors in the context of diabetes therapies, most notably insulin6" ;
    dmo:name "Medicines Prescribing and Administration Errors" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "medicines-prescribing-and-administration-errors" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "An ongoing cause of concern and a major risk factor for frail older people with diabetes is the incidence of prescribing and administration errors in the context of diabetes therapies, most notably insulin6" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/mixed-insulins> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Mixed Insulins" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "It has been reported that mixed insulins may convey a greater hazard than a background insulin (NPH or analogue) alone or in conjunction with a short acting insulin with meals11." ;
    dmo:name "Mixed Insulins" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "mixed-insulins" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "It has been reported that mixed insulins may convey a greater hazard than a background insulin (NPH or analogue) alone or in conjunction with a short acting insulin with meals11." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/moderate-to-severe-frailty> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Moderate to Severe Frailty" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "文档中明确指出该因素与延迟或失败出院、早期再入院相关" ;
    dmo:name "Moderate to Severe Frailty" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "moderate-to-severe-frailty" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "those with a history of repeated admissions for poor glucose control, hypoglycaemia, those with moderate to severe frailty, those with high comorbidity load, those with cognitive impairment and dementia who have still managed to remain in their own homes prior to admission, and those from residential care homes" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/more-sedentary-due-to-concurrent-illness> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "More Sedentary Due to Concurrent Illness" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Reduced physical activity due to illness can contribute to glucose elevation." ;
    dmo:name "More Sedentary Due to Concurrent Illness" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "more-sedentary-due-to-concurrent-illness" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "More sedentary due to concurrent illness" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/muscle-wasting> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Muscle Wasting" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Protein energy malnutrition and muscle wasting in CKD may lead to spontaneous resolution of hyperglycaemia and low HbA1c levels which requires regular review of hypoglycaemic medications." ;
    dmo:name "Muscle Wasting" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "muscle-wasting" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Protein energy malnutrition and muscle wasting in CKD may lead to spontaneous resolution of hyperglycaemia and low HbA1c levels which requires regular review of hypoglycaemic medications." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/muscle-weakness> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Muscle Weakness" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Older people with diabetes have an increased falls risk due to the presence of multiple risk factors1. Risk factors include: polypharmacy, muscle weakness, a history of a previous stroke, use of insulin, cognitive dysfunction, orthostatic hypotension, and visual loss2." ;
    dmo:name "Muscle Weakness" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "muscle-weakness" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk factors include: polypharmacy, muscle weakness, a history of a previous stroke, use of insulin, cognitive dysfunction, orthostatic hypotension, and visual loss2." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/no-knowledge-of-signs-and-symptoms-of-hypoglycaemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "No Knowledge of Signs and Symptoms of Hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "An England-wide care home diabetes audit showed that about 35% of residents had no knowledge of the signs and symptoms of hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:name "No Knowledge of Signs and Symptoms of Hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "no-knowledge-of-signs-and-symptoms-of-hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "An England-wide care home diabetes audit showed that about 35% of residents had no knowledge of the signs and symptoms of hypoglycaemia" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/not-usual-doctor> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Not Usual Doctor" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "A recent study in care homes showed that each care home resident was taking eight medicines each on average and on any single day 70% of the patients experienced at least one medication error because of inaccessible doctor, not usual doctor, work load pressure, lack of medication training, drug round interruptions, lack of team work among home practice and pharmacy and inefficient ordering system" ;
    dmo:name "Not Usual Doctor" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "not-usual-doctor" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "A recent study in care homes showed that each care home resident was taking eight medicines each on average and on any single day 70% of the patients experienced at least one medication error because of inaccessible doctor, not usual doctor, work load pressure, lack of medication training, drug round interruptions, lack of team work among home practice and pharmacy and inefficient ordering system" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/nutritional-deficits> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Nutritional Deficits" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Nutritional deficits have been reported in older hospitalised patients5" ;
    dmo:name "Nutritional Deficits" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "nutritional-deficits" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Nutritional deficits have been reported in older hospitalised patients5" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "A recent review of hospital diabetes management of older people identified multiple risk factors for hypoglycaemia many of which cluster in the frail older population, such as: dementia; renal insufficiency; and nutritional deficits9." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/older-age> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Older Age" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "文档聚焦于65岁及以上老年人群，明确指出该人群为脆弱群体，年龄本身为不可干预因素。" ;
    dmo:name "Older Age" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "NonModifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "older-age" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Age, frailty and diabetes - triple jeopardy for vulnerability to COVID-19 infection." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The largest absolute excess number of hospital admissions are in the older age group bands with 69% of excess admissions being in those over 55 years old" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Older people are also at increased risk of significant hypoglycaemia in hospital settings4" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "It has also been identified that hypoglycaemia in hospital: extends length-of-stay (LOS); is associated with increased cardiovascular events; increased risk of fracture inducing falls; and readmissions4-7." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "In the frail older patient intensive glucose control is contraindicated." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Percentage of older inpatients with diabetes, frailty and chronic kidney disease (CKD) receiving comprehensive geriatric assessment (CGA) including nutritional assessment in a single clinical unit or hospital ward in the past year" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/orthostatic-hypotension> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Orthostatic Hypotension" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Older people with diabetes have an increased falls risk due to the presence of multiple risk factors1. Risk factors include: polypharmacy, muscle weakness, a history of a previous stroke, use of insulin, cognitive dysfunction, orthostatic hypotension, and visual loss2." ;
    dmo:name "Orthostatic Hypotension" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "orthostatic-hypotension" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Risk factors include: polypharmacy, muscle weakness, a history of a previous stroke, use of insulin, cognitive dysfunction, orthostatic hypotension, and visual loss2." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/other-medication> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Other Medication" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Other medications such as warfarin, quinine, salicylates, fibrates, sulphonamides, MAO inhibitors, NSAIDs, probenecid, SSRIs can affect glucose levels." ;
    dmo:name "Other Medication" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "other-medication" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Warfarin, quinine, salicylates, fibrates, sulphonamides (including co-trimoxazole), monoamine oxidase inhibitors, NSAIDs, probenecid, SSRIs." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/peripheral-neuropathy> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Peripheral Neuropathy" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Peripheral neuropathy may play a major role in making this risk significant3 and thus assessment for peripheral neuropathy should be mandatory in the assessment of all inpatients with diabetes as suggested in the Diabetes UK document: putting feet first documents (e.g. Six Step Guide to improving Diabetes Footcare)4." ;
    dmo:name "Peripheral Neuropathy" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "peripheral-neuropathy" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Peripheral neuropathy may play a major role in making this risk significant3 and thus assessment for peripheral neuropathy should be mandatory in the assessment of all inpatients with diabetes as suggested in the Diabetes UK document: putting feet first documents (e.g. Six Step Guide to improving Diabetes Footcare)4." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/persistent-hyperglycaemia> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Persistent Hyperglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "People on insulin may be prone to hypoglycaemia and potentially nocturia will result from persistent hyperglycaemia, both of which may increase inpatient falls risk." ;
    dmo:name "Persistent Hyperglycaemia" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "persistent-hyperglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People on insulin may be prone to hypoglycaemia and potentially nocturia will result from persistent hyperglycaemia, both of which may increase inpatient falls risk." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/physical-inactivity> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Physical Inactivity" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Other factors that may lead to resolution of hyperglycaemia in CKD are gradual reduction of renal gluconeogenesis as renal function declines, physical inactivity and comorbid conditions6." ;
    dmo:name "Physical Inactivity" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "physical-inactivity" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Other factors that may lead to resolution of hyperglycaemia in CKD are gradual reduction of renal gluconeogenesis as renal function declines, physical inactivity and comorbid conditions6." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_15_frail_older_adult_with_diabetes_february_2023> .

